UPDATE companies SET description='Yost Foods is a family-owned custom ingredient manufacturer based in Brunswick, Ohio. Founded in 1991 by Bill Yost, the company began as an industrial food brokerage before evolving into a manufacturer of dry and wet ingredient systems for food producers.

The company produces custom dry blends — such as snack seasonings, dry sauces, and snack bases — and wet systems including marinades, sauces, hot sauces, purees, and kettle-cooked bases. Its facility features multiple production rooms separated by process type: liquid mixing for sauces and marinades, ribbon and paddle mixing for dry blends, and kettle cooking for caramelized sugars, purees, and pepper blends. Automation supports repeatable batches and scalable output from early-stage runs to high-volume production.

Yost serves national food manufacturers across categories including sauces, dressings, and marinades; refrigerated and ready-to-eat foods; frozen meals and pizzas; snacks, candy, and nuts; and ice cream and frozen desserts. The team works directly with R&D departments, food scientists, and culinary innovators to develop formulations that perform consistently in conventional and alternative product lines.

The company emphasizes collaborative development, technical expertise from food scientists and production specialists, fast sampling and rapid revisions, custom formulations with line-trial support, and consistency at scale through process control. It also provides clean-label and certification guidance for kosher, organic, gluten-free, non-GMO, and no-sugar-added claims, along with flexible packaging in bags, bag-in-box, drums, pails, and totes. A family-owned, long-term mindset drives a relationship-driven, accountable, and customer-first culture.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Excellent rating']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Liquid mixing for sauces, marinades, and hot sauces", "Ribbon and paddle mixing for dry blends and snack bases", "Kettle cooking for bases, caramelized sugar, purees, and pepper blends", "Custom dry ingredient systems (snack seasonings, dry sauces)", "Custom wet ingredient systems (marinades, sauces, purees)", "Scale-up and production runs", "Plant trials and process optimization", "Regulatory documentation and clean-label certification support (kosher, organic, gluten-free, non-GMO, NSA)", "Flexible packaging: bags, bag-in-box, drums, pails, totes", "Automation for repeatable batches and efficiency"], "industries": ["Sauces, dressings, and marinades", "Refrigerated and ready-to-eat foods", "Frozen meals and pizzas", "Snacks, candy, and nuts", "Ice cream and frozen desserts", "Food manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Collaborative development with R&D teams from concept through commercial launch", "Fast sampling, rapid revisions, and project management to keep timelines moving", "Custom formulations with reformulation and line-trial support", "SQF Excellent rating and regulatory documentation support", "Flexible packaging formats including bags, bag-in-box, drums, pails, and totes"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1991 by Bill Yost -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Brunswick, Ohio -> /about-us", "Started as industrial food brokerage, evolved into custom ingredient manufacturer -> /about-us", "Produces custom dry and wet ingredient systems -> /", "Processes: liquid mixing, ribbon/paddle mixing, kettle cooking -> /", "Multiple production rooms separated by process type -> /", "Automation for repeatable batches and scalable output -> /", "Serves sauces, dressings, marinades; refrigerated & ready-to-eat; frozen meals & pizzas; snacks, candy, nuts; ice cream & frozen desserts -> /", "Works with R&D teams, food scientists, culinary innovators -> /", "Collaborative development, technical expertise, speed to market, custom formulations, consistency at scale -> /", "Clean label & certification support: kosher, organic, gluten-free, non-GMO, NSA -> /", "Flexible packaging: bags, bag-in-box, drums, pails, totes -> /", "SQF Excellent rating -> /quality", "High-volume capacity, smart automation -> /", "Scale from early production to larger volumes -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "family-owned ingredient manufacturer that''s been creating custom dry and wet ingredient systems on an industrial scale since 1991", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='yost-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zen By Design was founded in 2001 in Scottsdale, Arizona, as a family-run venture dedicated to creating meditation furniture. The company began with the intention of bringing greater comfort and harmony to meditation practice, addressing the physical discomfort that often distracts practitioners during long sitting sessions.

The company handcrafts a line of meditation chairs—including the Tantra Chair, Anahata, Rama, Samurai, and the portable Zenfu zafu—as well as meditation candles. Each piece is built in Scottsdale from eco-friendly materials, with every wood component and fabric individually selected by artisans who have been with the company since its early years. Over more than two decades, Zen By Design has produced chairs for tens of thousands of meditators worldwide.

Notable clients have included Deepak Chopra, Andrew Weil, the Oprah Winfrey Show, Jack Canfield, and the Dalai Lama, though the company emphasizes its commitment to every customer regardless of prominence.

Zen By Design says its differentiators are ergonomic designs that provide sacral tilt and back support to encourage longer meditation, a family-oriented workplace that retains skilled artisans, and a 100 percent customer satisfaction policy with support available seven days a week, 365 days a year.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted furniture manufacturing", "Ergonomic design and prototyping", "Custom wood selection and finishing", "Custom fabric selection and upholstery", "Small-batch production", "Meditation cushion (zafu) manufacturing", "Candle production"], "industries": ["Meditation and mindfulness", "Wellness and spirituality", "Yoga", "Home furnishings", "Religious and spiritual institutions"], "materials": ["Eco-friendly wood", "Eco-friendly fabrics", "Sustainable materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted in Scottsdale, Arizona, USA using eco-friendly materials", "Ergonomic design with sacral tilt and back support for extended meditation", "Family-run operation with artisans retained since founding", "100% customer satisfaction guarantee with 7-day-a-week support", "Products used by prominent spiritual teachers and institutions worldwide"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db", "Headquarters Scottsdale, Arizona -> db", "Family-run venture -> /about", "Handcrafted in USA -> /", "Eco-friendly materials -> /", "Product line includes Tantra Chair, Anahata, Rama, Samurai, Zenfu, Zen Candle -> /", "Tens of thousands of customers worldwide over 21 years -> /", "Notable clients: Deepak Chopra, Andrew Weil, Oprah Winfrey Show, Jack Canfield, Dalai Lama -> /about", "Artisans from the beginning -> /about", "Ergonomic design with sacral tilt and back support -> /", "100% customer satisfaction, 7-day support -> /about", "Chairs in homes, ashrams, meditation centers globally -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our meditation seats and meditation furniture are handcrafted in Scottsdale, Arizona, USA", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zen-by-design' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zephyrus Electronics & Fabrication was founded in 1985 in Tulsa, Oklahoma. The company began as a combined electronics and metal fabrication shop, aiming to provide integrated manufacturing services.

The company operates two primary divisions: electronics manufacturing and metal fabrication. The electronics side offers in-house PCB design and assembly, wire cutting, stripping, and terminal pressing, plus custom wire harness assembly. The metal fabrication division runs a dedicated facility equipped with a Strippit 1000xp 20 CNC turret punch, an AMADA 8025 NC press brake, Miller Syncrowave 300 welders, and a Timesaver 22 series deburring and finishing system. Additional services include metal and plastic engraving using Gravograph IS7000/IS8000 and Epilog Laser Fusion systems, paint filling, and silk screening. The integrated setup allows rapid prototyping and quick turnaround on design changes.

Zephyrus serves original equipment manufacturers and industrial customers across a range of sectors, supplying custom control panels, complex wiring harnesses, and precision-machined enclosures. The company emphasizes a single-source model for complete build requirements.

Founded on a commitment to innovation, durability, and customer satisfaction, Zephyrus positions itself as a one-stop shop that streamlines production, reduces lead times, and ensures quality from concept to completion.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB design and assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Wire cutting and stripping", "Wire terminal pressing", "CNC turret punching", "Press brake forming", "Welding", "Deburring and surface finishing", "Metal engraving", "Plastic engraving", "Laser engraving", "Paint filling", "Silk screening"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Plastic", "Polycarbonate", "Metal"], "equipment": ["Schleuniger Eco Strip 9380 - wire cut and strip", "Molex 9002-50 - wire terminal press", "AMP Model G - wire terminal press", "RIGOL - digital oscilloscope", "Strippit 1000xp 20 - CNC turret punch", "AMADA 8025 - NC press brake", "Miller Syncrowave 300 - weld machines", "Timesaver 22 series - debur and surface finishing", "Gravograph IS7000 and IS8000 - metal and plastic engraving", "Epilog Laser Fusion - laser engrave metal and plastic", "Paintfill - of metal engraving"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single integrated supplier for electronics and metal fabrication", "In-house PCB design, assembly, wire harnessing, and enclosure fabrication", "Rapid prototyping and quick turnaround on changes", "End-to-end support from design to production"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1985 -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Tulsa, Oklahoma -> db", "Capabilities: PCB design and assembly, wire harnessing, metal fabrication, engraving, silk screening -> /", "Equipment: Schleuniger Eco Strip 9380, Molex 9002-50, AMP Model G, RIGOL oscilloscope, Strippit 1000xp 20, AMADA 8025, Miller Syncrowave 300, Timesaver 22 series, Gravograph IS7000/IS8000, Epilog Laser Fusion, Paintfill -> /", "Materials: plastic, polycarbonate, metal -> /", "Differentiators: one-stop integrated supplier, rapid prototyping, quick turn