UPDATE companies SET description='Zibtek was founded in 2009 in Salt Lake City, Utah. The company was established by entrepreneurs with experience founding, building, and exiting multiple businesses, though individual founders are not named in public materials.

The firm provides custom software development services including web and mobile application development, ERP development, API development, microservices architecture, and QA/QC support. It follows a practical agile methodology and offers staff augmentation — covering design, development, project management, DevOps, and testing — with resources available in‑country, nearshore, and offshore. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

Zibtek serves clients across healthcare technology (FormFox, an employee health and safety workflow provider), social media (Awsm, a private family‑group app), productivity software (Promptly Journals, a journaling app), and financial services (Academy Mortgage). The company emphasizes its local Utah presence for on‑site collaboration with regional businesses.

Zibtek states its differentiation lies in end‑to‑end product ownership, a rigorous hiring process that yields autonomous engineers, and a practical agile approach designed to reduce time‑to‑market while maintaining flexibility. The firm also highlights its local Salt Lake City base as a source of faster on‑site implementation and cost efficiency.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom software development", "Web application development", "Mobile app development", "ERP development", "API development", "Microservices architecture", "QA/QC support", "Staff augmentation", "Project management", "DevOps", "UI/UX design", "Strategic consulting", "React Native development", "Agile methodology implementation"], "industries": ["Healthcare technology", "Social media", "Productivity software", "Financial services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end product ownership", "Practical agile methodology", "Rigorous hiring process for autonomous engineers", "Local Salt Lake City presence for on-site collaboration", "Flexible staff augmentation across onshore, nearshore, offshore models"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 -> db", "Headquarters in Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Provides custom software development services -> page /", "Offers staff augmentation with onshore, nearshore, offshore options -> page /", "Clients include FormFox, Awsm, Promptly Journals, Academy Mortgage -> page /", "Uses practical agile methodology -> page /", "Provides full-cycle software development services -> page /", "End-to-end product ownership stated as differentiator -> page /", "Rigorous hiring process for top talent -> page /", "Local presence for on-site collaboration -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Zibtek delivers full-cycle software development services that meet your project requirements and business needs.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zibtek-software-company-in-salt-lake-city' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zim''s Bagging Company was founded in 1964 in Prichard, West Virginia. The business began as a converter and printer of film, foam, and bubble packaging materials and has operated continuously from its West Virginia location for six decades.

The company runs two production sites—a Main Facility and a SoftPack Facility—equipped for forming, folding, cutting, and sealing plastic film, foam, and bubble roll stock into bags and pouches. Its capabilities include flexographic printing up to 10 colors on a 59-inch web using a W&H Miraflex II press, as well as simpler line printing. Custom features such as tapes, handles, wickets, punched holes, labels, and bar codes can be added, and the firm offers photo-quality front-and-back printing on roll stock for automated form-and-fill lines. Core product lines encompass poly bags, wicket bags, PowerPack Mailer Bags, printed roll stock, and foam and bubble products.

Zim''s serves customers in automotive, e-commerce, food, home and garden, industrial, and medical markets, supplying custom packaging tailored to each sector''s requirements.

The company emphasizes its focus on value-added, non-standard packaging designs, citing more than 55 years of experience in the flexible packaging industry as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Film converting", "Foam converting", "Bubble packaging converting", "Flexographic printing (up to 10 colors)", "Line printing", "Bag forming", "Folding", "Cutting", "Heat sealing", "Wicketing", "Handle application", "Hole punching", "Label application", "Barcode printing", "Roll stock printing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "E-Commerce", "Food", "Home and Garden", "Industrial", "Medical"], "materials": ["Plastic film", "Foam", "Bubble roll-stock"], "equipment": ["W&H Miraflex II Printing Press (10-color, 59-inch web)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in value-added, custom-designed, non-standard packaging", "10-color, 59-inch web printing on a W&H Miraflex II press", "Two facilities (Main and SoftPack) for forming, folding, cutting, and sealing", "Custom options including tapes, handles, wickets, punched holes, labels, and bar codes", "Photo-quality front-and-back printing on roll stock for automated lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1964 -> db", "Headquarters Prichard, West Virginia -> db", "Converts and prints film, foam, bubble packaging materials -> /", "Two facilities: Main Facility and SoftPack Facility -> /", "Processes: forming, folding, cutting, sealing -> /", "Flexographic printing up to 10 colors, 59-inch web -> /", "W&H Miraflex II Printing Press -> /", "Custom options: tapes, handles, wickets, punched holes, labels, bar codes -> /", "Photo-quality front-and-back printing on roll stock -> /", "Product lines: poly bags, wicket bags, PowerPack Mailer Bags, printed roll stock, foam and bubble -> /", "Industries served: automotive, e-commerce, food, home and garden, industrial, medical -> /", "Differentiator: value-added, custom designed, non-standard packaging -> /", "Experience: 55+ years in flexible packaging -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1964, Zim''s Bagging Company has been converting and printing film, foam and bubble packaging materials.", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/zims-bagging-company/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zim-s-bagging-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Today the company operates as a global technology group headquartered in Premstaetten near Graz, Austria, with a co-headquarters in Munich, Germany, and a significant U.S. presence in Novi, Michigan. The business combines the legacy of OSRAM''s 120-year history with ams'' sensor expertise following their merger, creating a unified photonics powerhouse.

The group designs and manufactures semiconductor-based light emitters, optical sensors, CMOS integrated circuits, and supporting software, alongside traditional lighting technologies for automotive and specialty applications. Its product portfolio spans time-of-flight sensors such as the TMF8829 multi-zone dToF module, automotive signaling LEDs like the SYNIOS P2222, compact headlamp sources (OSLON Compact RM), addressable interior RGB devices (OSIRE E3030), infrared emitters for eye tracking, and VCSEL drivers for augmented reality. With approximately 18,500 employees worldwide, the company holds roughly 12,000 patents and patent applications and reported EUR 3.3 billion in revenue for 2025.

Customers span automotive and mobility (including interior lighting systems like ALIYOS and exterior signaling), medical and health (UV-C LED disinfection adopted by brands such as UPANG for baby bottle sterilizers), industrial automation, mobile and wearable devices, general lighting, and computing. The company cites collaborations with license partners to advance technological expertise across these sectors.

The company states its differentiation lies in "sensing the power of light" – harnessing the full spectrum, visible and invisible, to add intelligence to illumination. Its vision is to inspire people with innovative light and sensor solutions, while its mission emphasizes pioneering differentiating technologies that make the world safer, smarter, and more sustainable through long-term customer partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor-based light emitter fabrication", "Optical sensor design and manufacturing", "CMOS integrated circuit development", "Time-of-flight (ToF) sensor production", "VCSEL (Vertical-Cavity Surface-Emitting Laser) technology", "LED driver IC design", "Automotive signaling LED manufacturing", "Automotive interior lighting systems", "Infrared illumination for eye tracking", "UV-C LED disinfection technology", "LiDAR component development", "Projection device engineering", "Thin-film VCSEL fabrication", "Multi-zone distance sensing", "Addressable RGB LED packaging", "High-power forward lighting solutions"], "industries": ["Automotive & mobility", "Medical & health", "Industrial", "Mobile & wearables", "Lighting", "Computing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["12,000 patents and patent applications protecting core photonics IP", "Global manufacturing footprint with engineering excellence across semiconductor and lighting technologies", "Integrated portfolio spanning emitters, sensors, ICs, and software for complete photonics solutions", "EUR 3.3 billion annual revenue demonstrating scale and market adoption", "120-year heritage of light innovation combined with cutting-edge sensor expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1906 as OSRAM brand -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Premstaetten/Graz, Austria with co-headquarters in Munich, Germany -> /about-us", "U.S. presence in Novi, Michigan -> db", "Approximately 18,500 employees worldwide -> /about-us, db", "EUR 3.3 billion revenue in 2025 -> /about-us", "12,000 patents and patent applications -> /about-us", "Product portfolio: semiconductor-based light emitters, optical sensors, CMOS ICs, software, traditional lighting -> /about-us", "Specific products: TMF8829 ToF sensor, SYNIOS P2222 LED, OSLON Compact RM, OSIRE E3030, FIREFLY SFH 4030B, AS1181 driver IC -> /", "Industries served: Automotive & mobility, Medical & health, Industrial, Mobile & wearables, Lighting, Computing -> /, /about-us", "Customer example: UPANG uses UV-C LED for baby bottle sterilization -> /", "Vision: ''Inspire people with innovative light and sensor solutions'' -> /about-us", "Mission: ''Pioneer differentiating lighting and sensing technologies... make our world safer, smarter, and more sustainable'' -> /about-us", "Slogan: ''Sense the power of light'' -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a Photonics Powerhouse. Our distinct portfolio of advanced light and sensor technologies sets us apart in our industry. It includes high-quality semiconductor-based light emitters, optical sensors, CMOS ICs and software as well as a range of traditional lighting technologies for automotive and special applications.", "founded_year": "1906", "employee_count": "18500", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ams-osram' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1981 in Hayward, California, Pan Pacific Plastics Mfg Inc is a woman-owned and minority-certified packaging manufacturer. The company began as a domestic producer of paper and plastic bags and later expanded with overseas manufacturing partnerships across Asia.

The company manufactures and imports a full line of packaging, specializing in bags made from paper and plastic. At its Hayward facility, Pan Pacific performs plastic extrusion, printing, and converting in an expanded manufacturing plant. Through its Asian partnerships, it offers additional capacity for paper and plastic products. The firm maintains an in-house graphic art department for artwork proofs and design support, and operates quality control inspections at both factory and warehouse levels.

Pan Pacific serves a broad range of industries, including grocery, retail, promotional, industrial, agricultural, food service, airline, travel, and hospitality. Its customer base includes major distributors and various Fortune 500 companies, as well as small businesses and individual consumers worldwide.

Pan Pacific emphasizes complete control over every production step—domestically and overseas—to ensure quality and consistency. It differentiates itself with low domestic minimums (as little as 100 lbs of plastic), short domestic lead times of four to six weeks, price protection programs that lock in pricing for up to a year, and a responsive customer support model backed by over 100 years of combined staff experience.', certifications=ARRAY['National Minority Supplier Development Council (NMSDC) certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic extrusion", "Printing", "Converting", "Graphic design and artwork preparation", "Quality control and inspection", "Price protection programs", "Low minimum order quantities", "Domestic manufacturing", "Import sourcing and manufacturing partnerships", "Custom packaging design"], "industries": ["Grocery", "Retail", "Promotional", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Food service", "Airline", "Travel", "Hospitality"], "materials": ["Paper", "Plastic", "Polyethylene"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Domestic: 4-6 weeks; Import: 10-12 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete control over every production step domestically and overseas", "Low domestic minimums (as low as 100 lbs of plastic)", "Short domestic lead times (4-6 weeks)", "In-house graphic art department for artwork proofs and design", "Price protection programs guaranteeing prices and inventory up to a full year"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1981 -> db", "Headquartered in Hayward, California -> db", "Manufactures and imports packaging, specifically bags made from paper and plastic -> /about-us", "Plastic extruding, printing, and converting done in Hayward facility -> /about-us", "Manufacturing partnerships in Asia for unlimited paper and plastic products -> /about-us", "Woman-owned and minority-certified (NMSDC) -> /about-us", "Serves grocery, retail, promotional, industrial, agricultural, food service, airline, travel, hospitality industries -> /about-us", "Serves Fortune 500 companies -> /about-us", "Low domestic minimums as low as 100 lbs of plastic -> /", "Domestic lead times 4-6 weeks, import lead times 10-12 weeks -> /", "In-house graphic art department for artwork proofs -> /", "Quality control at factory and warehouse level -> /", "Price protection programs guaranteeing prices and inventory up to a full year -> /", "Complete control over every production step domestically and overseas -> /about-us", "Mission to provide quality service and products at competitive price -> /about-us", "100+ years of combined staff experience -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "In Hayward, CA we do all the plastic extruding, printing and converting in our expanded manufacturing facility.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "As low as 100 lbs of plastic", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pan-pacific-plastics-mfg-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='trueCABLE is based in Kansas City, Missouri. It operates as a brand supplying Ethernet and fiber optic connectivity products.

The company offers a range of networking infrastructure components, including bulk Ethernet cable (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6A), fiber patch cables, RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, patch panels, and installation tools such as crimpers, strippers, and punch-down tools. Products are built with solid bare-copper conductors and are tested to meet UL, ANSI/TIA, and U.S. safety standards. Part numbers such as 6ASCMRBLU_1Krl identify specific cable configurations.

Customers include data centers, commercial offices, industrial facilities, and residential installers. The company''s patch panels are marketed for data centers, offices, and industrial settings, while its bulk cable targets both home networks and commercial infrastructure. Coaxial cable is offered for low-voltage and satellite installations.

trueCABLE differentiates itself with same-day shipping on orders placed by 3 p.m. CT, a lifetime "Forever Warranty" on tools and cable, and a 30-day money-back guarantee. It emphasizes that its cable, connectors, and tools are validated as a complete system, and it provides educational resources through its Cable Academy.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS','UL Listed','ANSI/TIA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ethernet cable manufacturing (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6A)", "Fiber optic patch cable assembly (OS2, OM3, OM4)", "RJ45 connector termination (shielded/unshielded, pass-through, standard)", "Keystone jack manufacturing (punch-down, toolless, shielded/unshielded)", "Patch panel assembly (shielded/unshielded, 1U, 12/24 port, wall mount)", "Crimping and termination tool manufacturing", "Cable stripping and cutting tool manufacturing", "Punch-down tool manufacturing", "Quality testing and certification (UL, ANSI/TIA, RoHS)", "Same-day order fulfillment", "Warranty and returns management", "Technical education (Cable Academy)"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Commercial office construction", "Industrial facilities", "Residential networking", "Telecommunications", "Low-voltage installation", "Satellite installation"], "materials": ["Solid bare copper", "Fiber optic (single-mode OS2, multimode OM3/OM4)", "Coaxial cable"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for orders placed by 3pm CT", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on orders placed by 3 p.m. CT", "Lifetime \"Forever Warranty\" on cable and tools", "30-day money-back guarantee", "Cable, connectors, and tools tested as an integrated system", "Compliance with UL, ANSI/TIA, and RoHS standards"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Kansas City, Missouri -> db", "Product categories: bulk Ethernet cable, fiber patch cables, connectors, tools, patch panels -> /", "Same-day shipping for orders by 3pm CT -> /", "Forever Warranty and 30-day money-back guarantee -> /", "Products tested to exceed industry standards, comply with UL, ANSI/TIA, U.S. product safety standards -> /", "Certifications: RoHS, UL Listed -> db", "Materials: solid bare-copper conductors, fiber optic (OS2, OM3, OM4), coaxial cable -> /", "Industries: data centers, offices, industrial settings, commercial infrastructure, home networks, low-voltage, satellite -> /", "Part numbers example: 6ASCMRBLU_1Krl -> db", "Cable Academy educational resources -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our high-quality bulk Ethernet cables are available in Cat5e, Cat6, and Cat6A. Manufactured with solid, bare-copper conductors for better conductivity and flexibility.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='truecable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='10 Men Metal Fabrication operates from Omaha, Nebraska, where it was established in 2019 by owner Jaco Germishuys. The company began with a vision to serve as a one-stop shop for architectural sheet metal and custom fabrication across the Midwest, drawing on the combined decades of experience of its founding team.

The shop provides a full range of architectural metal fabrication services, including shearing, folding, welding, perforating, and metal finishing. Its product line covers standing seam roof panels, custom trim, vented ridge caps, column covers, cornice metal, gutters, downspouts, conductor heads, scuppers, flashings, copings, and specialty items such as copper and zinc countertops, backsplashes, and custom planters. The facility is described as a fully equipped metal shop, and the team has completed over 500 projects.

The company serves contractors, architects, homeowners, and DIY enthusiasts primarily throughout the Midwest. Its customer base spans the construction, architectural, roofing, and drainage industries, with projects ranging from standard architectural components to unique custom designs.

