UPDATE companies SET description='406 Processing & Taxidermy operates from Great Falls, Montana, where it runs a whole-animal butchery and taxidermy shop. The business is locally owned and operated by award-winning taxidermist Dylan Lencioni, an avid hunter and fisherman who frames the venture as a family endeavor. No founding year is disclosed in the available sources.

The company provides year-round processing for farmers, ranchers, and hunters. Its core services include wild-game processing (deer, elk, antelope), livestock slaughter and processing with an on-ranch harvesting option, European skull mounts cleaned using a beetle-based method that preserves bone integrity, and full taxidermy mounts produced by Brad Lencioni. The facility sits at 900 12th Street North; no square footage, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

The website lists set prices for European mounts — $195 for elk, $160 for deer — and notes that beetle cleaning is available for buffalo, bear, beef, and small game skulls.

The company emphasizes two differentiators: a guarantee that each client receives meat only from the animal they delivered, and the convenience of mobile on-ranch slaughtering. The beetle-cleaning process is highlighted as a way to maintain natural bone structure without shrinkage, and the taxidermy work is positioned as trophy-quality, using premium forms and materials.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Whole animal butchery", "Wild game processing (deer, elk, antelope)", "Livestock slaughter and processing", "On-ranch mobile slaughtering", "European skull mounts (beetle cleaning)", "Taxidermy mounting"], "industries": ["Agriculture (farmers and ranchers)", "Food processing (meat)", "Hunting and outdoor recreation", "Taxidermy"], "materials": ["Beef", "Deer", "Elk", "Antelope", "Buffalo", "Bear", "Small game"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Guaranteed return of meat from the customer''s own animal", "On-ranch slaughtering and transport to facility", "Beetle-based European skull cleaning preserving bone integrity", "Award-winning taxidermy using premium forms"], "facts_used": ["Location: Great Falls, Montana -> db", "Owner: Dylan Lencioni (award-winning taxidermist) -> /about", "Family-owned implication: ''from my family to yours'' -> /about", "Services: whole animal butchery, wild game processing, livestock processing, on-ranch slaughtering -> /", "European skull mounts with beetle cleaning -> /", "Taxidermy by Brad Lencioni -> /", "Pricing: Elk $195, Deer $160 for European mounts -> /", "Address: 900 12th Street N. Great Falls, MT 59401 -> /", "Guarantee of own meat return -> /about", "Locally owned business -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "406 Processing & Taxidermy is a whole animal butchery that provides year around services for farmers and ranchers including processing wild game during hunting season.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='406-processing-taxidermy' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='83 Woodworks LLC is a custom cabinetry and millwork shop based in Saco, Maine. The business was founded in 2020 by Troy Nadeau after a flower box he built for his wife attracted a buyer, turning a personal project into a dedicated workshop.

The company designs, fabricates, and installs custom cabinetry, CNC‑machined components, and architectural millwork. Its services span kitchens, bath vanities, built‑ins, closets, garage storage systems, home offices, and commercial millwork such as reception desks and fixtures. Projects move from concept through design to on‑site installation, all handled in‑house.

The primary clientele are homeowners throughout Southern Maine, with a growing commercial segment that includes businesses needing custom reception desks and retail fixtures. The shop serves both residential and light‑commercial markets across the region.

