UPDATE companies SET description='A Team Apparel operates from Prairie City, Iowa. The business was founded by husband-and-wife team Bruce and Cheryl Burkland, who aimed to assemble a crew of graphic designers and silkscreen printers. In 2026, Libby, founder of 515 Creative Designs (established 2018), acquired the company and merged it with her design firm to form 515 A*Team.

The shop specializes in custom-decorated apparel, offering screen printing, direct-to-film (DTF) heat transfers, and in-house graphic design. They source a wide range of garments—including ringspun cotton, tri-blend, performance polyester, fleece, and high-visibility safety wear—and handle orders from a 12-piece minimum for screen printing up to large volumes, with price breaks at 25, 37, 51, and 101 units. The company reports having designed and printed over one million shirts without missing a deadline.

A noted example is Crossroads of Pella, which relies on A Team Apparel for its annual Klompen Classic race T-shirts. The firm also serves clients requiring safety-compliant outerwear and corporate identity apparel.

