UPDATE companies SET description='AKAS Textiles & Laminations operates from Bensalem, Pennsylvania, where it was founded in 2007 as a closely-held enterprise. The company began with a mission to revive American textile manufacturing by sourcing every fiber domestically and partnering exclusively with U.S. mills, aiming to return pride and global leadership to the industry.

The company designs and manufactures high-performance fabrics, offering proprietary textiles for global clients and stocking first-quality roll goods of its own designs. Its capabilities span knitting and weaving, dyeing, laminating, backing, napping, cutting, printing, and applying specialized finishes for odor, stain, water resistance, and fire retardancy. An integrated supply chain eliminates middlemen, enabling low minimums and quick turnaround, while sustainable practices avoid harmful solvents and chemicals.

AKAS serves athletics, apparel, automotive, furniture, industrial, healthcare, hospitality, military, and food industries. Its fabrics have been used in space missions with U.S. astronauts, the Winter Olympics torch, and gear for the armed forces. Customers range from entrepreneurs like James McCrimmon (Draft Saver drink insulator) and Dr. David Pensak (Pensak Technologies) to strategic partners such as Dow, DuPont, and Invista, leveraging technologies like SILVADUR™, Teflon®, and Lycra®.

The company’s differentiation rests on its end-to-end domestic supply chain, over 100 years of combined experience in fiber engineering, and a personal commitment to quality that has driven double-digit annual growth since 2007. By controlling every step from raw material to finished roll, AKAS aims to deliver American-made textiles that meet mil-spec, food-safe, and flame-retardant standards.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL SPEC','Food-safe certification','Flame retardant certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Knitting/Weaving", "Dyeing", "Laminating", "Backing", "Napping", "Cutting", "Printing", "Odor-resistant finishes", "Stain-resistant finishes", "Water-resistant finishes", "Fire-retardant finishes", "Anti-microbial treatment", "Fabric design and consulting", "Raw material sourcing", "Supply chain management", "Quality control", "LEAN manufacturing", "Roll goods inventory", "Proprietary textile development", "Custom fabric engineering"], "industries": ["Athletics", "Apparel", "Automotive", "Furniture", "Industrial", "Healthcare", "Hospitality", "Military", "Food"], "materials": ["Yarns", "Cotton", "Synthetic fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Every fiber locally sourced and produced exclusively in American mills", "Green manufacturing with no harmful solvents or chemicals", "Integrated supply chain with no middlemen, offering low minimums and quick turnaround", "Over 100 years of combined experience in fiber engineering and textile fabrication", "Textiles qualified for space missions, Olympic use, and military gear"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Bensalem, Pennsylvania -> db", "Founded: 2007 -> db", "Mission to revive American textile manufacturing and partner exclusively with U.S. mills -> /about-us", "Closely-held enterprise with double-digit growth since 2007 -> /about-us", "Designs and manufactures high-performance fabrics, proprietary textiles, and stock roll goods -> /", "Processes: knittin