UPDATE companies SET description='ASM is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona. The company describes itself as a materials discovery company with nearly 60 years of materials innovation at its core, though a specific founding year is not disclosed in the provided materials. No founders are named, and ownership structure is not specified.

ASM designs and manufactures advanced wafer processing equipment for thin-film deposition, including atomic layer deposition (ALD), epitaxy, chemical vapor deposition (CVD), plasma-enhanced CVD (PECVD), surface preparation, and chemical mechanical polishing (CMP). The company also offers outcome-based service products aimed at improving uptime, yield, and performance in high-volume manufacturing. It employs over 4,800 people across 15 key locations worldwide and maintains long-term R&D partnerships with IMEC (since 1990) and the University of Helsinki (since 2003) to advance ALD processes and chemistries.

The company serves semiconductor manufacturers across logic/foundry, DRAM and HBM memory, advanced packaging, and interconnects. Its equipment and materials solutions support applications in AI data centers, next-generation healthcare, cloud computing, and energy-efficient devices. A concrete customer example cited in the materials is Intel, for which ASM innovations enabled critical components for copper interconnects.

ASM positions its differentiation on "atomistic control" and the ability to translate materials breakthroughs into manufacturable processes at scale. Its stated strategy focuses on maintaining share in ALD, growing in epitaxy and advanced packaging, expanding high-value service products, and accelerating sustainability through reduced precursor and energy consumption. The company has set financial targets of revenue exceeding €5.7 billion and an operating margin above 30% by 2030.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Atomic layer deposition (ALD)", "Epitaxy", "Chemical vapor deposition (CVD)", "Plasma-enhanced CVD (PECVD)", "Surface modification", "Surface preparation", "Chemical mechanical polishing (CMP)", "Chemistry innovation", "Surface engineering", "Outcome-based services", "Flowable Carbon technology", "Thin-film deposition"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Logic/foundry", "DRAM/HBM memory", "Advanced packaging", "Interconnects", "AI data centers", "Healthcare", "Cloud computing", "Energy-efficient devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Leading share in ALD for logic/foundry and DRAM/HBM memory", "AI/ML enabled common platform with novel chemistries to accelerate innovation", "Strength in chemistry innovation and surface engineering for advanced packaging", "Outcome-based service products that improve uptime, yield, and performance", "Targeting revenue >\u20ac5.7B and operating margin >30% by 2030"], "facts_used": ["HQ: Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Partnership with IMEC since 1990 -> description (db)", "Partnership with University of Helsinki since Dec 2003 -> description (db)", "4800+ employees worldwide -> /about page", "15 key locations -> /about page", "58 years of research -> /about page", "Advanced wafer processing equipment for thin-film deposition (ALD, epitaxy, CVD, surface modification) -> /about page", "Service products: outcome-based services