UPDATE companies SET description='AZ Metals operates from Mesa, Arizona, where it was founded in January 2011 by Doug and Jill Cone as a family‑owned and operated metal supply company. Doug Cone had worked in the metal industry since 1983, progressing from stacker to plant manager and franchise owner, while Jill Cone joined him in 2008 after a nursing career; together they launched AZ Metals after completing a prior franchise agreement.

The company stocks and distributes a wide range of metals — including carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, bronze, copper, and alloy and tool steels — in shapes such as sheet, plate, tube, pipe, bar, and structural profiles. It maintains over 19,000 line items and offers value‑added processing: shearing (Cincinnati 1810 and Pexto 12U52 squaring shears), band sawing (Hyd‑Mech S20 and Kama saws), punching and notching (GEKA Bendicrop 60S ironworker), bending (Chicago mechanical brake and Baileigh magnetic brake), drilling, and custom fabrication. All orders are cut to size with no minimum quantity.

AZ Metals serves residential, commercial, and industrial customers across the Phoenix East Valley and ships nationwide. Its client base includes builders, landscapers, repair and maintenance departments, fabrication shops, DIY enthusiasts, and local handymen.

The company’s stated mission is to meet the needs of both wholesale and retail buyers by providing an extensive selection of metals cut to size with exceptional service. It differentiates itself through no‑minimum‑order policies, same‑day local delivery, and the ability to source hard‑to‑find alloys.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal shearing", "Metal sawing", "Metal punching and notching", "Metal bending", "Metal drilling", "Custom metal fabrication", "Metal supply and distribution", "Cut\u2011to\u2011size services"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Industrial maintenance", "Landscaping", "Fabrication shops", "DIY/hobbyist"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Bronze", "Copper", "Alloy steel", "Tool steel"], "equipment": ["Cincinnati 1810 mechanical squaring shear", "Pexto Model 12U52 mechanical squaring shear", "Hyd\u2011Mech S20 mechanical band saw", "Kama band saw", "GEKA Bendicrop 60S Universal Ironworker", "Chicago mechanical finger brake", "Baileigh magnetic finger brake"], "volume": "Small bundles to production quantities", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order requirements", "Custom cut\u2011to\u2011size metals", "Over 19,000 line items stocked or sourced", "Daily local delivery and continental U.S. shipping", "Family\u2011owned with 40+ years of industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded January 2011 by Doug and Jill Cone -> /about-us", "Doug Cone in metal industry since 1983 -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Over 19,000 line items -> / (homepage)", "No minimum order requirements -> / (homepage)", "Shearing equipment: Cincinnati 1810, Pexto 12U52 -> / (homepage)", "Sawing equipment: Hyd\u2011Mech S20, Kama -> / (homepage)", "Punching/notching: GEKA Bendicrop 60S -> / (homepage)", "Bending: Chicago mechanical brake, Baileigh magnetic brake -> / (homepage)", "Materials: steel, stainless, aluminum, brass, bronze, copper, alloy/tool steel -> / (homepage)", "Industries served: residential, commercial, industrial, builders, landscapers, maintenance, fabricators, DIY -> / (homepage)", "Mission statement -> /about-us", "Local delivery and continental US shipping -> / (homepage)"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "AZ Metals specializes in both small bundle quantities of metal and larger production quantity orders. We are a steel and metal supplier... The metal cutting services we offer have expanded and we now offer custom metal fabrications!", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order requirements", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='az-metals' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='AZ Plastics, Inc. was founded in 2018 in Chicago Heights, Illinois, a south suburb of Chicago. The company was started by a team with extensive experience processing HDPE and HMW plastics, aiming to recycle used plastics into resin pellets as an eco-friendly substitute for virgin plastics.

The company operates a state-of-the-art facility where it buys used plastics — ranging from detergent bottles to industrial drums — and power washes, shreds, and converts them into pellets. It processes HDPE (high-density polyethylene) containers, plastic skids, injection-grade products, HDPE Frac Melt (milk jugs, shampoo bottles), and HMW (high molecular weight) plastics such as IBCs, drums, and pipes. The facility includes an in-house lab for quality assurance.

AZ Plastics serves a global customer base across North America, South America, Europe, and Asia. Its recycled resin pellets are used by manufacturers seeking sustainable alternatives for new plastic products. The company is a member of the Reusable Industrial Packaging Association (RIPA), indicating engagement with industrial packaging and recycling sectors.

