UPDATE companies SET description='Alcom LLC was founded in 2005 by Trapper Clark and Thomas Sturtevant in Waterville, Maine, where the company leased an 8,000-square-foot facility to begin building aluminum trailers. The operation soon relocated to a 70,000-square-foot plant in Winslow, Maine, which remains the corporate headquarters, and has since expanded to three additional manufacturing sites in Bonner, Montana; Sioux Falls, South Dakota; and Deland, Florida.

The company produces more than 160 standard trailer models spanning cargo, personal watercraft, horse and livestock, car hauler, snowmobile, landscape and utility, ATV, and motorcycle categories. The product line includes both open and enclosed configurations, with customization available for dealer-specific requirements.

Alcom sells exclusively through a dealer network that covers the United States and Canada, serving recreational and commercial end-users. Notable OEM partnerships include a licensed trailer line for Polaris Industries. The company''s dealer-first philosophy emphasizes rapid turnaround, dedicated territorial and inside sales teams, and ongoing model refinement to fill market gaps.

Alcom differentiates itself through speed and innovation: it introduced the industry''s first 100% aluminum livestock trailer chassis in 2016 and the only aluminum dump trailer in 2017. The leadership team, including CEO John Kwapis (appointed 2024) and CSMO Dan Mills (with the firm since inception), stresses operational stability and continuous investment in capacity, such as the 35,000-square-foot high-efficiency weld shop added in Winslow in 2019.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum welding and fabrication", "Trailer design and engineering", "Custom trailer manufacturing", "High-volume production (7-day operation)", "Licensed OEM manufacturing", "Open and enclosed trailer assembly"], "industries": ["Cargo trailers", "Personal watercraft (PWC) trailers", "Horse and livestock trailers", "Car haulers", "Snowmobile trailers", "Landscape and utility trailers", "ATV trailers", "Motorcycle trailers", "Commercial-grade trailers"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Operates manufacturing seven days a week for faster turnaround", "160+ standard trailer models across eight recreational and commercial categories", "Four U.S. manufacturing plants (ME, MT, SD, FL) reducing freight costs and lead times", "Dealer-first model with 13 territorial and 10 inside sales representatives", "Pioneered first 100% aluminum livestock trailer chassis (2016) and only aluminum dump trailer (2017)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 by Trapper Clark and Thomas Sturtevant -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Winslow, Maine -> /about-us, db", "Four manufacturing plants: Winslow ME, Bonner MT, Sioux Falls SD, Deland FL -> /about-us", "160+ standard trailer models across eight categories -> /about-us", "Employee count exceeds 700 nationwide (2021) -> /about-us", "Operates 7 days a week -> /about-us", "Dealer network in US and Canada -> /about-us", "Licensed trailer line for Polaris Industries (2010) -> /about-us", "First 100% aluminum livestock trailer chassis (2016) -> /about-us", "Industry''s only aluminum dump trailer (2017) -> /about-us", "Acquisitions: High Country Aluminum Trailers (2006), SnoPro Inc. (2009) -> /about-us", "Awards: Maine Small Business Persons of the Year (2010), #1 Market Share Growth enclosed trailers (2019) -> /about-us", "Leadership: John Kwapis CEO (Dec 2024), Dan Mills CSMO (since 2006) -> /about-us", "Facility sizes: Winslow 70k+35k sq ft, Bonner 170k+ sq ft, Sioux Falls 58k sq ft, Deland 130k sq ft -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we proudly manufactures 160+ standard trailer models", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "700+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alcom-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Aletheia Design & Sewing Service operates a low-overhead fashion factory in the Northeast Minneapolis arts district. Founded in 2014, the company is owned and operated by Abby Hansen, a garment technician with over 12 years of industrial apparel design and manufacturing experience. Hansen established the business to provide emerging brands with an affordable, manageable path from concept to production.

The shop specializes in contract cut-and-sew work for small-batch apparel, offering services a la carte: pattern making and auditing, fit audits, sample development, grading, marking, and production runs of 20 to 200 units per style per colorway. Equipment includes Union Special, Rimoldi, Juki, and Singer industrial sewing machines, along with dedicated cutting space. The facility is intentionally compact, focusing on the machinery and processes needed for efficient small-lot manufacturing.

Clients are primarily young, local, and small fashion brands launching their first lines or scaling early collections. Aletheia works collaboratively through a step-by-step development process that includes a launch audit, sourcing kickstart documents, and pre-production coordination.

The name “aletheia” (Greek for “disclosure” or “unconcealedness”) reflects Hansen’s stated vision of honesty in fashion. By keeping overhead low and limiting services to those she can execute efficiently, she aims to make domestic manufacturing accessible to brands that might otherwise be priced out of the market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract apparel cut and sew", "Sample making", "Product development", "Pattern making", "Pattern audit", "Fit audit", "Grading", "Marking", "Cut and bundle", "Marker making", "Small batch cut and sew (20-200 units)", "Sourcing kickstart document", "Launch audit consult", "General consulting", "Access to in-house trims and notions"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Fashion", "Emerging brands", "Small brands", "Local brands"], "materials": ["Fabrics", "Trims", "Notions", "Interfacing", "Snaps"], "equipment": ["Union Special sewing machines", "Rimoldi sewing machines", "Juki sewing machines", "Singer sewing machines", "Cutting space"], "volume": "20-200 units per style per colorway", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Headquarters Minneapolis, MN -> db and /about", "Owner Abby Hansen -> /about", "Services: contract cut and sew, sample making, product development -> /services", "Equipment: Union Special, Rimoldi, Juki, Singer -> /services", "Production volume 20-200 units -> /services", "Minimum order 20 units per style per colorway -> /services", "Collaborative product development model -> /services", "Low overhead factory -> /about", "Name meaning -> /about", "Location NE Minneapolis arts district -> /about", "Owner background: 12 years experience, certificate in Apparel Technologies, BA in Apparel Design -> /about", "Referral network for outside services -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Apparel Cut and Sew in Minneapolis, Minnesota", "founded_year": "2014", "employ